{"version":"2026.10.11-r25","id":"Q27109796","formula":"C₁₆H₁₈N₂O₂","hill":"C16H18N2O2","elements":["H","C","N","O"],"composition":{"C":16.0,"H":18.0,"N":2.0,"O":2.0},"names":{"en":"Clavicipitic acid"},"descriptions":{"en":"Clavicipitic acid is an ergoline-related compound found in ergot; it is a tricyclic indole alkaloid, but is in fact an amino acid that can be described as a specific structural analogue of lysergamide (ergine). Clavicipitic acid, a metabolite of Claviceps, is a mixture of isomers formed from tryptophan and mevalonic acid, but does not subsequently convert into the tetracyclic elymoclavine. Its formation represents a deviation in the biosynthesis of ergoline-based compounds following the first stage specific to this pathway, namely the isoprenylation of tryptophan."},"fame":1,"pubchemCid":10265155,"mass":270.33,"charge":0,"smiles":"CC(=CC1C2=C3C(=CNC3=CC=C2)CC(N1)C(=O)O)C","inchikey":"VZMAHZAQMKNJIG-UHFFFAOYSA-N","iupac":"9-(2-methylprop-1-enyl)-3,10-diazatricyclo[6.4.1.04,13]trideca-1,4,6,8(13)-tetraene-11-carboxylic acid","classes":[{"qid":"Q113145171","names":{"en":"type of chemical entity","ru":"тип химического объекта","uk":"тип хімічної сутності"}}],"structureInfo":{"kind":"molecule","source":"pubchem","ref":"10265155","atoms":38,"license":"PubChem (NIH), public data"},"structure":{"kind":"molecule","atoms":[{"x":2.639,"y":2.904,"z":-1.115,"el":"O"},{"x":2.842,"y":2.609,"z":1.136,"el":"O"},{"x":1.217,"y":0.447,"z":0.969,"el":"N"},{"x":-3.595,"y":1.125,"z":-0.518,"el":"N"},{"x":0.673,"y":-0.881,"z":0.624,"el":"C"},{"x":-1.671,"y":0.141,"z":0.056,"el":"C"},{"x":1.097,"y":1.46,"z":-0.083,"el":"C"},{"x":-0.172,"y":2.296,"z":0.083,"el":"C"},{"x":-1.444,"y":1.546,"z":-0.123,"el":"C"},{"x":-0.837,"y":-0.951,"z":0.408,"el":"C"},{"x":-3.03,"y":-0.083,"z":-0.18,"el":"C"},{"x":-2.651,"y":2.111,"z":-0.482,"el":"C"},{"x":-1.457,"y":-2.221,"z":0.522,"el":"C"},{"x":1.433,"y":-1.542,"z":-0.493,"el":"C"},{"x":-3.63,"y":-1.34,"z":-0.07,"el":"C"},{"x":2.279,"y